.{
    .name = .qmesh,
    .version = "0.2.1",
    .fingerprint = 0xc2bbdb284c1e27c5,
    .minimum_zig_version = "0.17.0",
    .dependencies = .{
        // Tarball pin, not a path: a `.path` dependency resolves against
        // the package directory, so a FETCHED qmesh (no sibling checkout)
        // failed to configure at all. The URL+hash form is what makes
        // qmesh consumable as a package. Same pin and same option map as
        // qmsg and nest, so one binary linking both packages shares ONE
        // quic module rather than compiling BoringSSL twice.
        // v0.32.0 (tag at ffdb251): three releases in one move, the set
        // (http3-zig, capnp-zig, qmsg, nest, mruby-quic) with it on
        // 2026-10-07 (v0.31.1 skipped as a step, not as content). No wire
        // change, no API change, the same option map. v0.31.0: a client
        // confirms the handshake on an ACK of its own 1-RTT packet, and
        // `Server.feed` leaves a `.dropped` datagram as it came (the
        // runner's second route copies before `feed` anyway). v0.31.1:
        // the idle timer follows RFC 9000 section 10.1, so a dead peer's
        // connection ends one idle timeout after the first probe, not
        // three. v0.32.0: the receive window an endpoint keeps open is the
        // one it announced (before, a fixed 1 MiB per stream and 16 MiB
        // per connection after the initial window): qmesh announces the
        // defaults for bidi streams and the connection, no change there;
        // its reliable unidirectional streams announce
        // `reliable_receive_window` (one `max_stream_message` by default),
        // which is now their window for life, not 1 MiB after the first
        // message: a long reliable stream moves one message size per
        // round trip unless the option is raised. Also
        // `max_buffered_send` on Connection, Client.Config and
        // Server.Config (the sender's window per stream, default 1 MiB,
        // qmesh sets none), 64 ACK ranges in a frame (was 16), and the
        // loss thresholds that widen for reordering shrink back after 16
        // clean round trips. Before it:
        // v0.30.1 (tag at ccf6ae2). Behavior only: no wire change, no API
        // change, the same option map. A probe timeout is not a loss (RFC
        // 9002 section 6.2.4: the Application space's probe timeout no
        // longer declares the oldest packet lost nor cuts the congestion
        // window; the probe carries its frames again, and the thresholds
        // decide when its ACK comes), and the handshake's probe timeout is
        // bounded at about a second, run from the last send. The doc of
        // `Server.feed` now says what qmesh 9b2a34c already relies on: the
        // bytes change in place whatever the outcome, so a `.dropped`
        // datagram routed to a dial needs a copy taken before `feed`.
        // `quic.unixWallClockUs` compiles on Zig 0.17.0, and
        // `Server.adoptLoopThread()` is new; qmesh calls neither. Not
        // v0.30.0: it did not compile on Windows. The set (http3-zig,
        // capnp-zig, qmsg, nest, mruby-quic) moved with it on 2026-10-06.
        // Before it:
        // v0.29.0 (tag at b9a15e6). It holds v0.25.0's security fix (one
        // short datagram from anyone who saw a packet of the connection,
        // or one a small receive buffer cut short, made
        // `Connection.handle` fail, and `Server.feed` closed the
        // connection; now such a packet is dropped) and v0.26.0's
        // repairs: a peer that leaves a connection ID out of its transport
        // parameters is refused, no handshake datagram is longer than 1200
        // bytes, a close during the handshake reaches the peer. v0.27.0
        // adds session tickets that live through a server restart; qmesh
        // sets none of the new fields. v0.28.0 keeps the end of a stream
        // that a `tick` reclaimed (`quic.app` reports `.fin` or `.reset`
        // for it, and a stream the app stopped ends as `.reaped`); qmesh
        // sets no `on_stream_end` hook. v0.28.1 is a 32-bit build fix.
        // v0.29.0: `Server.feed` makes no connection for a datagram of
        // which no packet opens and says `.dropped` (through v0.28.1 a
        // peer server's first flight made a half-open slot; the runner
        // gives a dial its own datagrams first all the same); a late
        // packet is not a lost packet; a connection costs about 91 KB of
        // heap (was 1.09 MB); a client connects through handshake loss;
        // a lost CONNECTION_CLOSE is sent again. No wire change. The
        // package accepts `optimize` too
        // (since v0.24.1), which the shared map does not pass. Since v0.24.0 there is no lifetime stream cap; the stream
        // limit is a window of streams open at once, and an id comes back
        // only when its stream is closed in both directions. qmesh opens
        // only unidirectional streams and finishes each one. Its floor is
        // the tagged Zig 0.17.0.
        // (`zig fetch --save` mangles these entries; edit by hand.)
        // v0.33.0 (2026-10-07): cluster A move; the quic release note has what changed.
        // v0.37.1 (2026-10-08): cluster A move; the quic release note has what changed.
        // v0.37.2 (2026-10-08): cluster A move; the quic release note has what changed.
        .quic = .{
            .url = "https://github.com/nullstyle/quic-zig/archive/refs/tags/v0.37.2.tar.gz",
            .hash = "quic-0.37.2-DnSYvb2bPwDUgMMPDFV3tX0CgvsCbn2u2ed60n4tUtZ-",
        },
        // LAN peer discovery for the qmesh-node binary only (`--mdns`).
        // Lazy: the library modules never import it, so a consumer that
        // fetched qmesh for `qmesh` / `qmesh_quic` never downloads it —
        // build.zig only resolves it after the dependency-build early
        // return. Same tarball form as quic, same "edit by hand" rule.
        // Option map is {target, optimize}; mdns-zig is std-only.
        .mdns = .{
            .url = "https://github.com/nullstyle/mdns-zig/archive/refs/tags/v0.1.1.tar.gz",
            .hash = "mdns-0.1.1-WRx6Po1rDwB0O0QRIhRkeWteVWKD-w7xTdKBJdFh2CJY",
            .lazy = true,
        },
    },
    // Consumer-facing archive. `sim/` ships because `qmesh_sim` is a
    // public module; `tests/` does not — the build returns early for
    // dependency builds, so downstream never configures them and
    // shipping them was pure fetch weight.
    .paths = .{
        "build.zig",
        "build.zig.zon",
        "src",
        "sim",
        "examples",
        "docs",
        "CHANGELOG.md",
        "LICENSE",
        "README.md",
    },
}
